      "message": "Both `cli.cc` (`BuildEcCommand`) and `cli_test.cc` (`BuildEcResponse`) manually calculate the packet checksum using a `for` loop and verbose pointer arithmetic. You can compress this elegantly using standard C++ algorithms.\n\nInclude `\u003cnumeric\u003e` at the top of both files, and replace the checksum generation logic with `std::accumulate` and direct vector indexing:\n\n**In `util/focaltech/cli.cc` (`BuildEcCommand`):**\n\n```\n-  uint8_t checksum \u003d 0;\n-  for (uint8_t b : packet) checksum +\u003d b;\n-\n-  uint8_t* checksum_ptr \u003d packet.data() + offsetof(ec_host_request, checksum);\n-  *checksum_ptr \u003d -checksum;\n+  uint8_t checksum \u003d std::accumulate(packet.begin(), packet.end(), uint8_t{0});\n+  packet[offsetof(ec_host_request, checksum)] \u003d -checksum;\n\n```\n\n**In `util/focaltech/cli_test.cc` (`BuildEcResponse`):**\n\n```\n-  uint8_t checksum \u003d 0;\n-  for (uint8_t b : packet) checksum +\u003d b;\n-\n-  const size_t checksum_offset \u003d offsetof(ec_host_response, checksum);\n-  packet[checksum_offset] \u003d -checksum;\n+  uint8_t checksum \u003d std::accumulate(packet.begin(), packet.end(), uint8_t{0});\n+  packet[offsetof(ec_host_response, checksum)] \u003d -checksum;\n\n```\n\n*(Note: Passing `uint8_t{0}` to `std::accumulate` ensures it safely wraps around at 256, which is exactly the behavior you want for this type of checksum).*",
