      "message": "Currently, `SendBulkDataOut` and `ReceiveBulkDataIn` accept the SCSI command as a `std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e scsi_cmd`. However, a USB Bulk-Only Transport (BOT) wrapper *strictly* requires exactly 16 bytes for the `cmd` array. By accepting a span, you lose the compile-time size guarantee—passing a smaller span would result in uninitialized bytes being read into the `BulkCbWrap`.\n\nSince your `BuildFtCmd` helper already returns an exact `std::array\u003cuint8_t, 16\u003e`, we can update the signatures to enforce this at compile time.\n\n**In `util/focaltech/ft_scsi.h`:**\n\n```\n // For sending data TO the device (Data buffer is const)\n std::expected\u003cvoid, Error\u003e SendBulkDataOut(\n-    const UsbDevice\u0026 device, std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e scsi_cmd,\n+    const UsbDevice\u0026 device, const std::array\u003cuint8_t, kScsiCmdSize\u003e\u0026 scsi_cmd,\n     std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e data_buffer, TransferDirection dir,\n     std::chrono::milliseconds timeout_ms);\n \n // For receiving data FROM the device (Data buffer is mutable)\n std::expected\u003cvoid, Error\u003e ReceiveBulkDataIn(\n-    const UsbDevice\u0026 device, std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e scsi_cmd,\n+    const UsbDevice\u0026 device, const std::array\u003cuint8_t, kScsiCmdSize\u003e\u0026 scsi_cmd,\n     std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e data_buffer, std::chrono::milliseconds timeout_ms);\n\n```\n\n*(Apply the exact same signature changes to the implementations in `ft_scsi.cc`)*",
