      "message": "Almost every single test in `usb_device_test.cc` repeats the exact same 3 lines to set up the mock and the device:\n\n```c\n  auto mock \u003d std::make_unique\u003cMockUsbTransport\u003e();\n  // setup mock...\n  UsbDevice device \u003d MakeDevice(std::move(mock));\n\n```\n\n**The Fix:** Use a Google Mock Test Fixture (`::testing::Test`) to automatically inject the mock and the device into every test, trimming significant boilerplate.\n\n**In `util/focaltech/usb_device_test.cc`:**\n\n```c\nclass UsbDeviceTest : public ::testing::Test {\n protected:\n  void SetUp() override {\n    auto m \u003d std::make_unique\u003cMockUsbTransport\u003e();\n    mock_ \u003d m.get(); // Keep a raw pointer for setting EXPECT_CALLs\n    device_ \u003d std::make_unique\u003cUsbDevice\u003e(std::move(m));\n  }\n\n  MockUsbTransport* mock_;\n  std::unique_ptr\u003cUsbDevice\u003e device_;\n};\n\n```\n\nYou can then simplify all tests by swapping `TEST` to `TEST_F`, allowing them to focus purely on the logic:\n\n```\n-TEST(UsbDeviceTest, SendForwardsToTransport) {\n-  auto mock \u003d std::make_unique\u003cMockUsbTransport\u003e();\n+TEST_F(UsbDeviceTest, SendForwardsToTransport) {\n   std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e test_data \u003d {0x01, 0x02, 0x03};\n   auto timeout \u003d 100ms;\n \n-  EXPECT_CALL(*mock, Send(ElementsAreArray(test_data), timeout))\n+  EXPECT_CALL(*mock_, Send(ElementsAreArray(test_data), timeout))\n       .WillOnce(Return(test_data.size()));\n \n-  UsbDevice device \u003d MakeDevice(std::move(mock));\n-  auto result \u003d device.Send(test_data, timeout);\n+  auto result \u003d device_-\u003eSend(test_data, timeout);\n   ASSERT_TRUE(result.has_value());\n   EXPECT_EQ(*result, test_data.size());\n }\n\n```",
